          "kind": "text",
          "text": "The test file adds a lifecycle-test purpose comment and imports Bun test tools, file and hashing helpers, model identity, a client type and the process classes. The test file creates a temporary directory with a harness-specific prefix for its fake worker fixtures. The test file registers an afterAll hook that recursively removes its temporary directory with force enabled. The test file adds a helper that returns a hexadecimal SHA-256 digest of text for fake-worker identity fields. The fakeWorker helper writes a Python ready-message and request-loop fixture and returns its launch configuration with the generated script hash. The answer fixture emits a flushed reranked reply with the request ID, a score of 0.5 and a false truncation flag for each document, plus fixed timing and memory fields. The test checks scoring before exit, rejection after exit and close, replacement of a failed reranker, and retention of that replacement after cleanup of the old instance. The test holds one manually counted call open beyond a 50-millisecond idle interval, expects no encoder closure, then ends the call and expects one closure after a further wait "
