        "after": "The new module names the idle-exit and dead-reranker scenarios and imports the tools needed to exercise them with fake workers. Its imports do not themselves establish those lifecycle guarantees, and no test run is recorded. Module loading creates a fresh directory under the system temporary directory. The fake-worker helper writes Python files into that directory and uses it as its snapshot path; no execution proof is recorded. Once the file's tests finish, Bun invokes a hook that removes the temporary workspace and everything inside it. The force option tolerates an absent target; no record…",
